WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.228 --> 00:00:03.395
(upbeat guitar music)

00:00:13.727 --> 00:00:16.514
- Hi, I'm Hannah, your
friendly neighborhood wine mom

00:00:16.514 --> 00:00:17.996
and if you're anything
like me, you believe

00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:20.763
that a glass of wine at eight
PM makes you a better mom.

00:00:20.763 --> 00:00:22.702
So pour yourself a glass and let's talk.

00:00:22.702 --> 00:00:23.870
Tonight, we're drinking rose,

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.623
because I'm always drinking rose.

00:00:26.623 --> 00:00:28.041
What else am I gonna drink?

00:00:28.041 --> 00:00:29.153
Rose all day.

00:00:29.153 --> 00:00:31.353
A topic that runs rampant in the comments

00:00:31.353 --> 00:00:33.929
of all of these videos is discipline.

00:00:33.929 --> 00:00:35.888
How do I discipline kids?

00:00:35.888 --> 00:00:38.003
How do I deal with difficult children?

00:00:38.003 --> 00:00:41.533
So tonight's topic, the
best way to discipline kids.

00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:43.967
And I know because I am a certified mom.

00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:47.855
I have been certified by the
board of certifiers of moms.

00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:49.437
First, context.

00:00:49.437 --> 00:00:51.390
Whenever I'm about to punish my children,

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.247
I have to make the decision,

00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:56.391
are they misbehaving or are
they just acting their age?

00:00:56.391 --> 00:00:57.632
My oldest son is four.

00:00:57.632 --> 00:00:59.362
He likes to do stuff himself.

00:00:59.362 --> 00:01:02.036
He likes to get his own glasses of water.

00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:03.081
That's his new thing.

00:01:03.081 --> 00:01:05.135
So he gets on his little step stool

00:01:05.135 --> 00:01:08.526
and gets water out of the
filtered spout next to our sink,

00:01:08.526 --> 00:01:10.605
but he always fills his water cup

00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:12.938
up to the very top of the brim,

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:14.892
and then he spills it everywhere

00:01:14.892 --> 00:01:16.941
so there's puddles of
water all over the house

00:01:16.941 --> 00:01:18.717
whenever he tries to get his own water.

00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:20.063
But I'm not gonna punish him for that

00:01:20.063 --> 00:01:22.129
because he's four and that's normal.

00:01:22.129 --> 00:01:24.560
On the other hand, if he
thinks I'm not looking,

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.114
he'll give his younger
brother a big shove.

00:01:27.114 --> 00:01:29.645
Kids need to learn that we see everything,

00:01:29.645 --> 00:01:32.033
so I know that that's
happening and I see it,

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:33.556
and he will get in trouble for that

00:01:33.556 --> 00:01:36.629
because spilling water, just being a kid.

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.962
Pushing your brother, just being a jerk.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:43.973
Sounds like bumping music outside.

00:01:45.179 --> 00:01:46.766
What?

00:01:46.766 --> 00:01:49.425
There are like a bunch of
crazy teens in my neighborhood.

00:01:49.425 --> 00:01:50.424
That's normal.

00:01:50.424 --> 00:01:52.813
They're gonna blast their
music to a douche-y level.

00:01:52.813 --> 00:01:54.303
Next, what?

00:01:54.303 --> 00:01:56.877
I never use the one two three method.

00:01:56.877 --> 00:01:58.461
I've done it several times,

00:01:58.461 --> 00:02:00.237
and I'll get all the way to three

00:02:00.237 --> 00:02:02.687
but I realize that I
haven't thought it out

00:02:02.687 --> 00:02:05.545
to even figure out what's gonna
happen when I get to three,

00:02:05.545 --> 00:02:08.462
so when I do, it's just like, okay.

00:02:09.722 --> 00:02:11.325
It totally loses its effectiveness

00:02:11.325 --> 00:02:13.758
if there's no follow through
on what's gonna happen

00:02:13.758 --> 00:02:15.759
so instead, I bought this shirt

00:02:15.759 --> 00:02:18.035
and it had this phrase on it that I read

00:02:18.035 --> 00:02:20.473
and was just like, this
really speaks to me,

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:24.850
and it says, "I say what,
not because I didn't hear you

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.637
"but because I'm giving you a chance

00:02:26.637 --> 00:02:28.473
"to change what you just said."

00:02:28.473 --> 00:02:29.829
It's in very small letters.

00:02:29.829 --> 00:02:33.181
And so I say that to every
crappy thing my kid says.

00:02:33.181 --> 00:02:35.982
He'll be like, you're the meanest mom ever

00:02:35.982 --> 00:02:38.893
when I don't give him three
cookies instead of two,

00:02:38.893 --> 00:02:41.232
and I'll turn around and be like, "What?"

00:02:41.232 --> 00:02:43.518
And he's like, oh, I'm just kidding.

00:02:43.518 --> 00:02:45.005
These two cookies are great.

00:02:45.005 --> 00:02:46.767
It gives them a chance
to correct themselves

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:49.162
before they get punished, which
I think is very important.

00:02:49.162 --> 00:02:51.838
My hand is making it warm.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.583
I have to hold onto the stem.

00:02:53.583 --> 00:02:54.594
I've seen that in the comments.

00:02:54.594 --> 00:02:57.485
People are like, hold the stem
and the wine won't get warm.

00:02:57.485 --> 00:02:58.638
Thank you.

00:02:58.638 --> 00:02:59.885
Next, lead by example.

00:02:59.885 --> 00:03:01.486
I always try to act in the way

00:03:01.486 --> 00:03:03.307
that I expect my children to act.

00:03:03.307 --> 00:03:05.865
I want them to use manners,
so I always use manners

00:03:05.865 --> 00:03:07.210
when I'm interacting with them.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:09.209
If I ask them to do
something, I'll say please.

00:03:09.209 --> 00:03:10.637
If they do it, I say thank you.

00:03:10.637 --> 00:03:12.553
I see a lot of parents who don't do that

00:03:12.553 --> 00:03:14.586
and they just kind of
bark orders at their kids

00:03:14.586 --> 00:03:17.464
and expect them to use
manners and be polite,

00:03:17.464 --> 00:03:18.625
and I don't think that's right.

00:03:18.625 --> 00:03:21.267
If I'm talking to my
husband, I'll say, hi,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:24.139
how was your day, how are
you doing, what's going on?

00:03:24.139 --> 00:03:27.146
And so when I come home from
work and I see my four year old

00:03:27.146 --> 00:03:30.060
the first thing he asks me
is, how was your day, mom?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.637
And it's just the most heartwarming thing.

00:03:32.637 --> 00:03:34.588
Can you believe a four
year old is asking me

00:03:34.588 --> 00:03:37.073
and cares enough, but
it's because he sees it

00:03:37.073 --> 00:03:39.997
in the way that his parents
behave with other people.

00:03:39.997 --> 00:03:42.815
If on top of that, he came
up to me with a glass of wine

00:03:42.815 --> 00:03:45.307
and said, hey, mom, how was your day?

00:03:45.307 --> 00:03:46.579
That would just be...

00:03:46.579 --> 00:03:47.580
I'm just kidding.

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.519
I'm not gonna teach my
kid to pour wine for me.

00:03:49.519 --> 00:03:51.388
Next, offer choices.

00:03:51.388 --> 00:03:54.510
I'll offer him choices of
two things he doesn't like,

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:57.506
and therefore, he will
feel like he's in control

00:03:57.506 --> 00:04:00.766
but still ends up doing both
things that he doesn't like.

00:04:00.766 --> 00:04:03.345
Do you wanna brush your
teeth first or take a bath?

00:04:03.345 --> 00:04:06.164
Do you wanna eat this carrot
first or this broccoli first?

00:04:06.164 --> 00:04:07.328
He gets to pick.

00:04:07.328 --> 00:04:09.209
You pick whatever piece of crap you want.

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:12.170
This is some low key
manipulation that I like to do,

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:14.174
and I'm pretty sure that this is a tactic

00:04:14.174 --> 00:04:16.384
they use in the FBI or something like that

00:04:16.384 --> 00:04:17.776
when they're interrogating people,

00:04:17.776 --> 00:04:19.967
but it works just as well for kids.

00:04:19.967 --> 00:04:22.108
And sometimes, there
are the rare instances

00:04:22.108 --> 00:04:25.010
when the child will say
something like, neither.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.366
I don't wanna do either one.

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.782
I don't wanna take a bath, I
don't wanna brush my teeth.

00:04:28.782 --> 00:04:30.508
I don't wanna eat carrots,
I don't wanna eat broccoli.

00:04:30.508 --> 00:04:33.675
And that's when you pull out the what.

00:04:34.925 --> 00:04:39.092
It all fits together in this
intricate web of discipline.

00:04:40.169 --> 00:04:42.119
No burps this episode.

00:04:42.119 --> 00:04:43.663
Next, go easy on yourself.

00:04:43.663 --> 00:04:47.134
Yeah, I want my kids to
be disciplined properly,

00:04:47.134 --> 00:04:50.445
but in a situation where
I'm about to lose my shit,

00:04:50.445 --> 00:04:52.382
I gotta give up, I gotta
throw in the towel,

00:04:52.382 --> 00:04:54.723
raise the white flag, whatever.

00:04:54.723 --> 00:04:57.120
As a parent, you're not
gonna win every battle

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.291
and that's fine.

00:04:58.291 --> 00:05:01.205
Nobody's perfect, no kid is
perfect, no parent is perfect.

00:05:01.205 --> 00:05:02.784
No discipline is perfect,

00:05:02.784 --> 00:05:07.359
which leads us to our very
final and ultimate rule

00:05:07.359 --> 00:05:09.527
when it comes to disciplining kids.

00:05:09.527 --> 00:05:12.881
Don't take unsolicited advice
from complete strangers.

00:05:12.881 --> 00:05:16.333
There's so many parents who
are willing to just like

00:05:16.333 --> 00:05:19.696
bark their discipline tactics as truth,

00:05:19.696 --> 00:05:22.900
and that's not true because
each child is different.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.077
Every parent is different.

00:05:24.077 --> 00:05:26.469
Every relationship is different.

00:05:26.469 --> 00:05:29.391
Everything is different
as far as what works,

00:05:29.391 --> 00:05:32.819
and if you're about to share
this video with the caption,

00:05:32.819 --> 00:05:35.463
"Oh, she doesn't know
anything about discipline,

00:05:35.463 --> 00:05:36.801
"this doesn't work,"

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.898
jokes on you because I really don't.

00:05:38.898 --> 00:05:40.447
What do I know?

00:05:40.447 --> 00:05:41.515
I don't know your kids.

00:05:41.515 --> 00:05:43.634
I don't know you, I don't know anything.

00:05:43.634 --> 00:05:46.159
This is the discipline
method that works for me.

00:05:46.159 --> 00:05:47.282
It might not work for you.

00:05:47.282 --> 00:05:48.969
It might work for somebody else.

00:05:48.969 --> 00:05:50.478
Bottom line with discipline,

00:05:50.478 --> 00:05:52.939
if what you have is
working, keep doing it,

00:05:52.939 --> 00:05:54.077
unless you're spanking your kids

00:05:54.077 --> 00:05:55.726
because that shit is really weird.

00:05:55.726 --> 00:05:58.222
Just save that for the bedroom.

00:05:58.222 --> 00:06:01.449
I'm sorry, y'all, but
I really do love you.

00:06:01.449 --> 00:06:02.773
So that's all I've got for today.

00:06:02.773 --> 00:06:05.478
I'm Hannah, your friendly
neighborhood wine mom

00:06:05.478 --> 00:06:07.904
and if there's a method of discipline

00:06:07.904 --> 00:06:09.320
that particularly works for you,

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:12.769
whether you're a babysitter
or a nanny or a parent

00:06:12.769 --> 00:06:15.312
or whatever you are,
leave it in the comments.

00:06:15.312 --> 00:06:17.680
But be nice, 'cause if you're not nice,

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:18.853
we can't be best friends.

00:06:18.853 --> 00:06:21.187
See what I did there with
my discipline method?

00:06:21.187 --> 00:06:25.733
If you do this, then you
can't have this, right?

00:06:25.733 --> 00:06:28.965
So I'm probably going
to finish this little

00:06:28.965 --> 00:06:30.821
what's left of rose,

00:06:30.821 --> 00:06:32.597
and go have a dance party with my husband

00:06:32.597 --> 00:06:35.174
because that's what cool parents do.

00:06:35.174 --> 00:06:36.424
Till next time.

00:06:43.814 --> 00:06:46.136
It's easier without a glass.

00:06:46.136 --> 00:06:48.969
I don't like washing wine glasses.

